<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- Dark band at the bottom edge fading up to transparent so the
         overlaid title + metadata stay legible over bright thumbnail art
         (e.g. the yellow "OTRA TURRA" frames). angle=90 runs bottom→top.

         The curve is deliberately STEEP: near-opaque exactly where the text
         sits (bottom edge), then falling away faster than before. This is a
         PARETO move over the previous #CC/#59 curve — DARKER at the bottom
         (90% vs 80%), which is what buys the title its own ground when a clip
         carries its own burned-in captions right where our title lands (the
         on-device collision case), and LIGHTER at the midpoint (30% vs 35%),
         so the "dark smear over half the tile" this curve was softened for
         can only improve, never regress.

         That smear was reported on the light generated mime thumbnails (audio
         tiles). Those are now the scrim-LESS card branch in the adapters, but
         a QUEUED / in-progress / errored audio tile still renders on this
         scrim — which is why the midpoint stays low rather than returning to
         the old #EE/#99 (~60% at midpoint). The text's own drop shadow carries
         the rest. -->
    <gradient
        android:angle="90"
        android:startColor="#E6000000"
        android:centerColor="#4D000000"
        android:endColor="@android:color/transparent" />
</shape>
